  <section><h2>Frequently asked questions about window replacement in Richardson</h2>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Who is the best window replacement company in Richardson, TX?</h3><p>For 2026, our top pick is Southern Windows &amp; Doors, a family-owned company with a physical Richardson address on Columbia Dr and 49-plus years in business. Window World of Dallas, also based in Richardson, is a strong second option as a national brand with a local branch.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Why do so many Richardson homes still have single-pane windows?</h3><p>Much of Richardson's housing stock dates to the 1960s-70s tract-home boom around neighborhoods like Prairie Creek and Canyon Creek, and many of those homes still carry their original single-pane aluminum-frame windows, which offer far less insulation than modern double-pane units.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>How much does window replacement cost in Richardson?</h3><p>Full-house replacement typically runs $8,000-$20,000 across North Texas depending on window count and glass package, while single-window replacements run roughly $400-$1,200 installed depending on size and frame material.</p></div>
    <div class="rv-q"><h3>Does replacing windows help with Richardson's summer heat?</h3><p>Yes. Upgrading from original single-pane aluminum windows to modern double-pane, low-E units meaningfully cuts solar heat gain, which matters in a city where summer highs routinely clear 100 degrees and AC accounts for a large share of the electric bill.</p></div>
